1. SCOPE AND DEFINITIONS

"Software" means project-owned source, documentation, original artwork and
other material supplied under these terms, including modified versions.
Separately identified third-party material is excluded. "Licensor" means the
copyright holders offering this material. "You" means the individual exercising
these permissions. "Upstream" means the Upstream Project above or its publicly
designated successor maintained by the project maintainers.

"Personal Noncommercial Use" means use by a natural person in their individual
capacity for private study, experimentation, education, entertainment or hobby
activities, without an anticipated commercial purpose or direct or indirect
commercial advantage. It excludes use on behalf of an employer, client,
business or other organisation, even if the Software itself is not sold.

"Modification" means any change, adaptation, patch, translation, port or
derivative work of the Software. "Integration" means code You create or adapt
specifically to embed, link, wrap, extend or expose its functionality, including
purpose-built plugins, connectors and API, MCP or IPC adapters. Merely running
unmodified general-purpose operating systems, browsers, editors, build tools,
CAD tools or MCP clients alongside it is not an Integration. Ordinary project
files, driver data, measurements, prompts and generated designs are not
Modifications or Integrations merely because the Software processes them.

"Corresponding Source" means the preferred form for modifying all of Your
Modifications and Integration code, including relevant changes to a containing
application You author or control, necessary build scripts, dependency/version
information and reproduction instructions. It excludes unrelated independent
components, separately licensed third-party components, credentials, personal
information and user data. Supply configuration templates instead of secrets.

2. LIMITED PERMISSION

Subject to every condition below, Licensor grants You nonexclusive, worldwide,
royalty-free permission to obtain, run, study, copy and modify the Software,
create Integrations and redistribute it solely for Personal Noncommercial Use.
Redistribution must be without charge, preserve these terms and attribution,
identify changes and supply Corresponding Source under this same licence.
Recipients receive permission from Licensor under these terms. You may not
offer project-owned code on more permissive terms.

3. NO COMMERCIAL OR ORGANISATIONAL USE

These permissions exclude commercial use or redistribution, internal business
use, paid or business-related services, consulting, SaaS, commercial research
or development, and using the Software to design or produce goods or designs
intended for sale. An organisation's use is not permitted merely because it is
nonprofit, educational or publicly funded. Such use requires separate written
permission from the relevant rights holders. Public source availability does
not imply commercial permission.

4. MANDATORY PUBLICATION AND UPSTREAM SUBMISSION

For every Modification or Integration, You must commit and publish complete
Corresponding Source in a publicly readable repository, without a paywall,
under this same licence, and submit it to Upstream as a pull request with an
intelligible description, reproduction instructions and the public source URL.
Preserve copyright/licence notices and identify Your changes.

These duties apply even if You keep the work for personal use and do not
distribute it. Complete them before use beyond local development/testing,
before redistribution or making the work available to another person, and
in every case within 30 calendar days of making the Modification/Integration.
Local development/testing within that period is permitted only for Personal
Noncommercial Use and does not waive the duty to contribute.

A public fork and PR satisfy submission; direct write access is not required.
Maintainers need not review, accept or merge Your proposal. Submission is not
endorsement. Keep Corresponding Source publicly available for as long as You
use or distribute the affected work. If Upstream is unavailable or technically
cannot accept PRs, publish source and a patch/integration proposal in Your
public repository, record the unavailable submission, and submit when Upstream
becomes available. Public publication remains required. A declined, closed or
unavailable PR never grants a permanent right to keep changes private.

5. CONTRIBUTIONS AND MAINTENANCE

Contribute only material You have the right to license. Submission licenses
Your contribution to recipients under these terms and grants Upstream
maintainers an irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free copyright permission to
incorporate, run, test, modify, maintain, publish and redistribute it as part of
this project under this same licence. Maintainers may act for the project
organisation. This grants neither general commercial-use permission nor
permission to relicense Your contribution commercially. You retain ownership;
no copyright assignment is required. Separately identified third-party material
retains its own licence and must be compatible with its proposed use.

6. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL, OUTPUTS AND BRANDING

Restrictions apply only to rights Licensor can grant in project-owned material.
Third-party code/assets retain their own licences and notices; nothing here
removes rights their authors independently grant. See docs/THIRD-PARTY.md.

You retain rights in independent user data and generated designs. Ordinary
generated CAD, mesh, numerical and report files do not trigger contribution
back. Licensor permits use and sharing of project-owned boilerplate emitted
automatically into such outputs as part of those outputs without that duty.
This exception does not authorise commercial use of the Software or copying
its implementation into another application.

No general trademark permission is granted. Reasonable attribution and display
of the original identity in permitted copies are allowed. Clearly identify
modified versions; do not suggest endorsement of a fork or integration.

